@startuml card-api-clients
!include plantuml-style.puml
title API-fed card examples - no automatic laser execution
hide footbox
actor User
participant "Card CLI / neocv" as Client
participant "Laser API" as API
participant Browser
participant "Actual laser" as Laser

Client -> API: GET /api, /api/templates, /api/materials, /api/assets
API --> Client: Contract; definitions, dimensions, public asset IDs
alt Wi-Fi card
  Client -> API: POST /api/jobs/review\nNetwork QR + optional public label
else vCard / contact card
  Client -> API: POST /api/jobs/review\nvCard/CV URL front + optional public tiger back
else GitHub recovery card
  Client -> API: POST /api/jobs/review\nRecovery payload QR front + login URL QR back
end
API -> API: Validate template and side bindings\nCompose separate guide/front/back pixels in RAM
API --> Client: Review ID; projected fields; per-side exact PNG/SVG
note over Client,API
  CLI examples use fictional data only; text-file overrides stay in RAM.
  The producer supplies vCard serialization, logo asset reference and recovery QR payload.
  Recovery codes are never a printed text element.
  Captions identify the recovery-card front and login-card back; URL text is optional.
  Submission does not open serial or move the laser.
end note
User -> Browser: Open laser UI
Browser -> API: GET /api/state and /api/jobs/review
API --> Browser: Current API-submitted review
User -> Browser: Review front/back; confirm placement; Burn front
Browser -> API: POST /api/plan then /api/run (front)
API -> Laser: Approved front raster (Real mode only)
Laser --> API: Status or accepted 90-second silence assumption
API --> Browser: Software outcome, not physical acceptance
User -> Browser: Inspect front; OK observation
Browser -> API: POST /api/verdict
User -> User: Confirm stopped; flip; seat back in SAME guide
User -> Browser: Confirm flipped placement; Burn back
Browser -> API: POST /api/plan\nreview ID, back stage, placement_confirmed=true
API -> API: Require prior accepted stages in current mode
Browser -> API: POST /api/run (separate operator action)
API -> Laser: Approved back raster
API --> Browser: Status/outcome; await user observation
note over User,Laser
  Optional markings add a separate first stage on bare backing.
  STOP/errors never authorize automatic retry or a side change.
  No new real-device run is authorized by this example.
end note
@enduml